{
    "chapter_num": 3,
    "verses_count": 16,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Qualifications of Bishops"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The saying is sure: If any one aspires to the office of bishop, he desires a noble task. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now a bishop must be above reproach, the husband of one wife, temperate, sensible, dignified, hospitable, an apt teacher, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "no drunkard, not violent but gentle, not quarrelsome, and no lover of money. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "He must manage his own household well, keeping his children submissive and respectful in every way; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "for if a man does not know how to manage his own household, how can he care for God’s church? "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "He must not be a recent convert, or he may be puffed up with conceit and fall into the condemnation of the devil;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or slanderer"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "moreover he must be well thought of by outsiders, or he may fall into reproach and the snare of the devil."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or slanderer"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Qualifications of Deacons"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Deacons likewise must be serious, not double-tongued, not addicted to much wine, not greedy for gain; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "they must hold the mystery of the faith with a clear conscience. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And let them also be tested first; then if they prove themselves blameless let them serve as deacons. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The women likewise must be serious, no slanderers, but temperate, faithful in all things. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Let deacons be the husband of one wife, and let them manage their children and their households well; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "for those who serve well as deacons gain a good standing for themselves and also great confidence in the faith which is in Christ Jesus."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Mystery of Our Religion"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "I hope to come to you soon, but I am writing these instructions to you so that, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "if I am delayed, you may know how one ought to behave in the household of God, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and bulwark of the truth. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Great indeed, we confess, is the mystery of our religion:"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "He"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Greek Who; other ancient authorities read God; others, Which"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " was manifested in the flesh,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "vindicated"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or justified"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " in the Spirit,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "\tseen by angels,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "preached among the nations,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "believed on in the world,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "\ttaken up in glory."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}